    "description": "This dataset provides monthly unemployment statistics for the European Union, disaggregated by sex and age group, covering the period from January 1983 to July 2020 (latest available version). The data originates from Eurostat, based on the indicator Unemployment by sex and age - monthly data within the Euro SDMX Metadata Structure (ESMS) framework. Unemployment is presented across three age categories: TOTAL (all ages), Y_LT25 (under 25 years), and Y25_74 (ages 25-74). Data are further broken down by sex, with T representing the total population, M for males, and F for females. Two measurement units are used: PC_ACT for unemployment as a percentage of the active population, and THS_PER for the number of unemployed persons in thousands. The dataset enables detailed analysis of long-term labor market trends, including youth unemployment, gender disparities, and the impact of economic cycles on different demographic groups. It is an essential resource for researchers, policymakers, and economists studying employment dynamics and social inequality within the European Union.",
